The close policy relies only on `Quorvex___get_approval`, because its output values are declared as enums. `Halvern___get_approval` returns free-form strings with no declared values, so I can't tell what counts as a person's approval from it. It is permitted as a read-only lookup but never satisfies the close condition.

I wrote the enum values in `output.decision` and `output.approver_kind` as entity UIDs, since the schema declares them as enum entities rather than strings. If your validator expects plain string literals there instead, that is the one line to change.

